STEP 1: Headless Service + StatefulSet
--------------------------------------
vi sts-web.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: web
spec:
  clusterIP: None
  selector:
    app: web
  ports:
  - port: 80
---
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: StatefulSet
metadata:
  name: web
spec:
  serviceName: web
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: web
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: web
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:1.27
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
        volumeMounts:
        - name: data
          mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html
  volumeClaimTemplates:
  - metadata:
      name: data
    spec:
      accessModes: ["ReadWriteOnce"]
      resources:
        requests:
          storage: 1Gi

Terminal 2: k get pods -l app=web -w
k apply -f sts-web.yaml

Watch: web-0 Running and Ready BEFORE web-1 starts, then web-2.


STEP 2: Per-pod PVCs
--------------------
k get pvc
  data-web-0, data-web-1, data-web-2

Write a unique page into each pod's own disk:
for i in 0 1 2; do
  k exec web-$i -- sh -c "echo 'I am web-$i' > /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html"
done


STEP 3: Stable DNS names
------------------------
k run tmp --rm -it --image=busybox:1.36 -- sh
  nslookup web                 # returns 3 pod IPs (headless)
  wget -qO- web-0.web
  wget -qO- web-1.web
  wget -qO- web-2.web.default.svc.cluster.local
  exit


STEP 4: Delete a pod: same name, same disk
------------------------------------------
k get pod web-1 -o wide          # note IP and node
k delete pod web-1
k get pod web-1 -o wide          # same NAME, new IP
k exec web-1 -- cat /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html   # "I am web-1"

The new web-1 re-attached data-web-1.


STEP 5: Scale down and up
-------------------------
k scale sts web --replicas=1     # web-2 deleted first, then web-1
k get pods,pvc                    # PVCs data-web-1/2 still exist!
k scale sts web --replicas=3
k exec web-2 -- cat /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html   # "I am web-2" again


STEP 6: Rolling update with partition (canary)
----------------------------------------------
k patch sts web -p '{"spec":{"updateStrategy":{"type":"RollingUpdate","rollingUpdate":{"partition":2}}}}'
k set image sts/web nginx=nginx:1.26
k rollout status sts/web
k get pods -l app=web -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,IMAGE:.spec.containers[0].image

Only web-2 updated. Lower the partition to roll out further:
  k patch sts web -p '{"spec":{"updateStrategy":{"rollingUpdate":{"partition":0}}}}'
  k rollout status sts/web
Updates go web-1, then web-0 (highest to lowest).


STEP 7: A real database: PostgreSQL StatefulSet
-----------------------------------------------
k create secret generic pg --from-literal=POSTGRES_PASSWORD=pgpass

vi sts-postgres.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: pg
spec:
  clusterIP: None
  selector: {app: pg}
  ports:
  - port: 5432
---
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: StatefulSet
metadata:
  name: pg
spec:
  serviceName: pg
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels: {app: pg}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {app: pg}
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: postgres
        image: postgres:16
        envFrom:
        - secretRef:
            name: pg
        env:
        - name: PGDATA
          value: /var/lib/postgresql/data/pgdata
        ports:
        - containerPort: 5432
        volumeMounts:
        - name: pgdata
          mountPath: /var/lib/postgresql/data
  volumeClaimTemplates:
  - metadata:
      name: pgdata
    spec:
      accessModes: ["ReadWriteOnce"]
      resources:
        requests:
          storage: 1Gi

(PGDATA points to a subfolder because the mount root contains
"lost+found" on some storage types, which postgres refuses.)

k apply -f sts-postgres.yaml
k rollout status sts/pg
k exec -it pg-0 -- psql -U postgres -c "create table t(x text); insert into t values('survives');"
k delete pod pg-0
k rollout status sts/pg
k exec -it pg-0 -- psql -U postgres -c "select * from t;"     # survives


STEP 8: Deleting a StatefulSet keeps PVCs
-----------------------------------------
k delete sts web pg
k get pvc            # all still there
k delete svc web pg
k delete pvc --all   # now the data is gone
k delete secret pg


